{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1114","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1114"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options passed into the SDK and further piped to the AI provider."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tprovideroptionssuperset","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TProviderOptionsSuperset"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TProviderOptionsSuperset"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":"> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tprovideroptionsformodel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TProviderOptionsForModel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TProviderOptionsForModel"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TProviderOptionsSuperset"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tcontext","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TContext"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TContext"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"abortcontroller","children":[{"type":"text","value":"abortController?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional abortController?: AbortController;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1219","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1219"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AbortController for request cancellation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Allows you to cancel an in-progress request using an AbortController.\nUseful for implementing timeouts or user-initiated cancellations."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const abortController = new AbortController();\nsetTimeout(() => abortController.abort(), 5000); // Cancel after 5 seconds\nawait chat({ ..., abortController });","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortController"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"agentloopstrategy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"agentLoopStrategy?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional agentLoopStrategy?: AgentLoopStrategy;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1142","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1142"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"approvals","children":[{"type":"text","value":"approvals?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional approvals?: ReadonlyMap<string, boolean>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1277","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1277"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client approval decisions for this run, keyed by approval id. The engine\npopulates this from approvals carried on the incoming messages. Harness\nadapters consult it to resolve "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ask"},{"type":"text","value":"-policy permission requests (the agent\npauses on a risky action; the client re-runs with a decision recorded\nhere). Undefined for direct adapter usage outside the chat engine."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"capabilities","children":[{"type":"text","value":"capabilities?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional capabilities?: CapabilityContext;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1268","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1268"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware capability context for this run. The engine populates it with\nthe live middleware context so harness adapters that declare\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires: [SomeCapability]"},{"type":"text","value":" can read provided capabilities from inside\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatStream"},{"type":"text","value":" — e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSandbox(options.capabilities)"},{"type":"text","value":". Capabilities are\nprovisioned by middleware "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup"},{"type":"text","value":" before the adapter runs. Undefined for\ndirect adapter usage outside the chat engine."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"context","children":[{"type":"text","value":"context?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional context?: TContext;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1126","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1126"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime context provided by the caller and passed to middleware and\nserver-side tool implementations."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"conversationid","children":[{"type":"strike","children":[{"type":"text","value":"conversationId?"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional conversationId?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1205","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1205"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"deprecated","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":" instead. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"conversationId"},{"type":"text","value":" is the legacy\npre-AG-UI name for the same concept (a stable per-conversation\nidentifier used to correlate client/server devtools events). When\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"conversationId"},{"type":"text","value":" is omitted, the runtime falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":"\nautomatically, so most callers can simply pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":" (or rely\non "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatParamsFromRequest"},{"type":"text","value":", which surfaces it on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Will be removed in a future major release."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"lazytoolsconfig","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lazyToolsConfig?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional lazyToolsConfig?: LazyToolsConfig;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1153","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1153"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional configuration for lazy-tool discovery (tools marked "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lazy: true"},{"type":"text","value":").\nTunes how much of each lazy tool's description appears in the discovery\ncatalog. Optional — defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ includeDescription: 'none' }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"logger","children":[{"type":"text","value":"logger"}]},{"type":"code","value":"logger: InternalLogger;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1226","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1226"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Internal logger threaded from the chat entry point. Adapter implementations\nmust call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"logger.request()"},{"type":"text","value":" before SDK calls, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"logger.provider()"},{"type":"text","value":" for each\nchunk received, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"logger.errors()"},{"type":"text","value":" in catch blocks."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"messages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"messages"}]},{"type":"code","value":"messages: ModelMessage<\n  | string\n  | ContentPart<unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown>[]\n  | null>[];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1120","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1120"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"metadata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"metadata?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional metadata?: Record<string, any>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1164","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1164"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observability metadata attached to this call. Surfaced to middleware,\ndevtools, and the event client; values may be arbitrarily structured\n(objects, arrays). Adapters never forward this field onto the provider\nwire request."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To send provider-side request metadata, use the provider's\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" field instead, where the provider supports one (e.g.\nOpenAI's and OpenRouter's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" are both Record<string, string>)."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"model","children":[{"type":"text","value":"model"}]},{"type":"code","value":"model: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1119","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1119"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"modeloptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"modelOptions?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional modelOptions?: TProviderOptionsForModel;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1165","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1165"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"outputschema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"outputSchema?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional outputSchema?: SchemaInput;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1194","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1194"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema for structured output."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two distinct use sites:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User-facing (activity layer):"}]},{"type":"text","value":" accepts any\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/SchemaInput.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SchemaInput"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Zod, ArkType, Valibot, or a raw JSON Schema.\nThe activity layer converts to JSON Schema before handing off."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter-facing ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatStream"},{"type":"text","value":" call):"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the engine populates this with\na pre-converted JSON Schema "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"only"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when the adapter declared\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema(modelOptions) === true"},{"type":"text","value":". The adapter\nshould then wire the schema into the upstream request (e.g.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"response_format: { type: 'json_schema', ... }"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text.format"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"output_format"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json-schema"},{"type":"text","value":") alongside any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How the engine then takes the object depends on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"combinedStructuredOutputSource()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'text'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default): the final-turn assistant text is the JSON."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'event'"},{"type":"text","value":": the adapter emits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" during\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatStream"},{"type":"text","value":". Accumulated prose is not parsed."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters that did NOT declare the capability never see this field\npopulated — the engine instead invokes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredOutput"},{"type":"text","value":" /\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredOutputStream"},{"type":"text","value":" after the agent loop."}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parentrunid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"parentRunId?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional parentRunId?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1243","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1243"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parent run ID for AG-UI protocol nested run correlation.\nSurfaced for observability/middleware; not consumed by the LLM call."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"request","children":[{"type":"text","value":"request?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional request?: Request | RequestInit;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1166","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1166"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resume","children":[{"type":"text","value":"resume?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional resume?: RunAgentResumeItem[];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1258","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1258"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI interrupt resume responses supplied by the client on a follow-up run.\nA first-party generic item carries the original request in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runId?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional runId?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1238","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1238"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run ID for AG-UI protocol run correlation.\nWhen provided, this will be used in RunStartedEvent and RunFinishedEvent.\nIf not provided, a unique ID will be generated."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional state?: unknown;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1252","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1252"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Application state mirrored in a STATE_SNAPSHOT before an interrupt terminal."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"subagentrunid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"subagentRunId?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional subagentRunId?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1249","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1249"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AG-UI subagent run id when this chat runs as a child of another run.\nA child "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.subagentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":". Middleware reads it as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.subagentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":". Absent on a top-level run."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"systemprompts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"systemPrompts?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional systemPrompts?: SystemPrompt[];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1141","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1141"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"System prompts to include with the request."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accepts plain strings (the common case) or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ content, metadata }"},{"type":"text","value":"\nobjects that let providers attach typed metadata (e.g. Anthropic\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cache_control"},{"type":"text","value":" for prompt caching) per prompt. At the chat call site\nthe adapter narrows "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":"'s type via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"~types['systemPromptMetadata']"},{"type":"text","value":"\n— providers that don't declare one default to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never"},{"type":"text","value":", which makes the\nfield carry no meaningful value (TypeScript will only accept\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" there). Provider-foreign metadata that reaches an adapter\nvia JS / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"as any"},{"type":"text","value":" is silently dropped, never written to the wire."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"see-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SystemPrompt"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"threadid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"threadId?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional threadId?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1232","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1232"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thread ID for AG-UI protocol run correlation.\nWhen provided, this will be used in RunStartedEvent and RunFinishedEvent."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toolexecution","children":[{"type":"text","value":"toolExecution?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional toolExecution?: \"parallel\" | \"sequential\";","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1147","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1147"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How the server tools of one model turn run. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'parallel'"},{"type":"text","value":" (the default)\nstarts them together, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'sequential'"},{"type":"text","value":" runs them one at a time."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tools?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional tools?: AnyTool[];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1121","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1121"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tprovideroptionssuperset","text":"TProviderOptionsSuperset","level":3},{"id":"tprovideroptionsformodel","text":"TProviderOptionsForModel","level":3},{"id":"tcontext","text":"TContext","level":3},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"abortcontroller","text":"abortController?","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":4},{"id":"agentloopstrategy","text":"agentLoopStrategy?","level":3},{"id":"approvals","text":"approvals?","level":3},{"id":"capabilities","text":"capabilities?","level":3},{"id":"context","text":"context?","level":3},{"id":"conversationid","text":"conversationId?","level":3},{"id":"deprecated","text":"Deprecated","level":4},{"id":"lazytoolsconfig","text":"lazyToolsConfig?","level":3},{"id":"logger","text":"logger","level":3},{"id":"messages","text":"messages","level":3},{"id":"metadata","text":"metadata?","level":3},{"id":"model","text":"model","level":3},{"id":"modeloptions","text":"modelOptions?","level":3},{"id":"outputschema","text":"outputSchema?","level":3},{"id":"parentrunid","text":"parentRunId?","level":3},{"id":"request","text":"request?","level":3},{"id":"resume","text":"resume?","level":3},{"id":"runid","text":"runId?","level":3},{"id":"state","text":"state?","level":3},{"id":"subagentrunid","text":"subagentRunId?","level":3},{"id":"systemprompts","text":"systemPrompts?","level":3},{"id":"see-2","text":"See","level":4},{"id":"threadid","text":"threadId?","level":3},{"id":"toolexecution","text":"toolExecution?","level":3},{"id":"tools","text":"tools?","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1114](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1114)\n\nOptions passed into the SDK and further piped to the AI provider.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TProviderOptionsSuperset\n\n`TProviderOptionsSuperset` *extends* `Record`\\<`string`, `any`\\> = `Record`\\<`string`, `any`\\>\n\n### TProviderOptionsForModel\n\n`TProviderOptionsForModel` = `TProviderOptionsSuperset`\n\n### TContext\n\n`TContext` = `unknown`\n\n## Properties\n\n### abortController?\n\n```ts\noptional abortController?: AbortController;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1219](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1219)\n\nAbortController for request cancellation.\n\nAllows you to cancel an in-progress request using an AbortController.\nUseful for implementing timeouts or user-initiated cancellations.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst abortController = new AbortController();\nsetTimeout(() => abortController.abort(), 5000); // Cancel after 5 seconds\nawait chat({ ..., abortController });\n```\n\n#### See\n\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortController\n\n***\n\n### agentLoopStrategy?\n\n```ts\noptional agentLoopStrategy?: AgentLoopStrategy;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1142](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1142)\n\n***\n\n### approvals?\n\n```ts\noptional approvals?: ReadonlyMap<string, boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1277](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1277)\n\nClient approval decisions for this run, keyed by approval id. The engine\npopulates this from approvals carried on the incoming messages. Harness\nadapters consult it to resolve `ask`-policy permission requests (the agent\npauses on a risky action; the client re-runs with a decision recorded\nhere). Undefined for direct adapter usage outside the chat engine.\n\n***\n\n### capabilities?\n\n```ts\noptional capabilities?: CapabilityContext;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1268](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1268)\n\nMiddleware capability context for this run. The engine populates it with\nthe live middleware context so harness adapters that declare\n`requires: [SomeCapability]` can read provided capabilities from inside\n`chatStream` — e.g. `getSandbox(options.capabilities)`. Capabilities are\nprovisioned by middleware `setup` before the adapter runs. Undefined for\ndirect adapter usage outside the chat engine.\n\n***\n\n### context?\n\n```ts\noptional context?: TContext;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1126](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1126)\n\nRuntime context provided by the caller and passed to middleware and\nserver-side tool implementations.\n\n***\n\n### ~~conversationId?~~\n\n```ts\noptional conversationId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1205](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1205)\n\n#### Deprecated\n\nUse `threadId` instead. `conversationId` is the legacy\npre-AG-UI name for the same concept (a stable per-conversation\nidentifier used to correlate client/server devtools events). When\n`conversationId` is omitted, the runtime falls back to `threadId`\nautomatically, so most callers can simply pass `threadId` (or rely\non `chatParamsFromRequest`, which surfaces it on `params`).\n\nWill be removed in a future major release.\n\n***\n\n### lazyToolsConfig?\n\n```ts\noptional lazyToolsConfig?: LazyToolsConfig;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1153](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1153)\n\nOptional configuration for lazy-tool discovery (tools marked `lazy: true`).\nTunes how much of each lazy tool's description appears in the discovery\ncatalog. Optional — defaults to `{ includeDescription: 'none' }`.\n\n***\n\n### logger\n\n```ts\nlogger: InternalLogger;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1226](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1226)\n\nInternal logger threaded from the chat entry point. Adapter implementations\nmust call `logger.request()` before SDK calls, `logger.provider()` for each\nchunk received, and `logger.errors()` in catch blocks.\n\n***\n\n### messages\n\n```ts\nmessages: ModelMessage<\n  | string\n  | ContentPart<unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown>[]\n  | null>[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1120](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1120)\n\n***\n\n### metadata?\n\n```ts\noptional metadata?: Record<string, any>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1164](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1164)\n\nObservability metadata attached to this call. Surfaced to middleware,\ndevtools, and the event client; values may be arbitrarily structured\n(objects, arrays). Adapters never forward this field onto the provider\nwire request.\n\nTo send provider-side request metadata, use the provider's\n`modelOptions` field instead, where the provider supports one (e.g.\nOpenAI's and OpenRouter's `metadata` are both Record<string, string>).\n\n***\n\n### model\n\n```ts\nmodel: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1119](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1119)\n\n***\n\n### modelOptions?\n\n```ts\noptional modelOptions?: TProviderOptionsForModel;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1165](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1165)\n\n***\n\n### outputSchema?\n\n```ts\noptional outputSchema?: SchemaInput;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1194](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1194)\n\nSchema for structured output.\n\n**Two distinct use sites:**\n\n1. **User-facing (activity layer):** accepts any\n   [SchemaInput](../type-aliases/SchemaInput.md) — Zod, ArkType, Valibot, or a raw JSON Schema.\n   The activity layer converts to JSON Schema before handing off.\n\n2. **Adapter-facing (`chatStream` call):** the engine populates this with\n   a pre-converted JSON Schema **only** when the adapter declared\n   `supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema(modelOptions) === true`. The adapter\n   should then wire the schema into the upstream request (e.g.\n   `response_format: { type: 'json_schema', ... }`, `text.format`,\n   `output_format`, `--json-schema`) alongside any `tools`.\n\n   How the engine then takes the object depends on\n   `combinedStructuredOutputSource()`:\n   - `'text'` (default): the final-turn assistant text is the JSON.\n   - `'event'`: the adapter emits `structured-output.complete` during\n     `chatStream`. Accumulated prose is not parsed.\n\n   Adapters that did NOT declare the capability never see this field\n   populated — the engine instead invokes `structuredOutput` /\n   `structuredOutputStream` after the agent loop.\n\n***\n\n### parentRunId?\n\n```ts\noptional parentRunId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1243](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1243)\n\nParent run ID for AG-UI protocol nested run correlation.\nSurfaced for observability/middleware; not consumed by the LLM call.\n\n***\n\n### request?\n\n```ts\noptional request?: Request | RequestInit;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1166](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1166)\n\n***\n\n### resume?\n\n```ts\noptional resume?: RunAgentResumeItem[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1258](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1258)\n\nAG-UI interrupt resume responses supplied by the client on a follow-up run.\nA first-party generic item carries the original request in `metadata`.\n\n***\n\n### runId?\n\n```ts\noptional runId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1238](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1238)\n\nRun ID for AG-UI protocol run correlation.\nWhen provided, this will be used in RunStartedEvent and RunFinishedEvent.\nIf not provided, a unique ID will be generated.\n\n***\n\n### state?\n\n```ts\noptional state?: unknown;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1252](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1252)\n\nApplication state mirrored in a STATE_SNAPSHOT before an interrupt terminal.\n\n***\n\n### subagentRunId?\n\n```ts\noptional subagentRunId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1249](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1249)\n\nAG-UI subagent run id when this chat runs as a child of another run.\nA child `chat()` passes `ctx.subagentRunId`. Middleware reads it as\n`ctx.subagentRunId`. Absent on a top-level run.\n\n***\n\n### systemPrompts?\n\n```ts\noptional systemPrompts?: SystemPrompt[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1141](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1141)\n\nSystem prompts to include with the request.\n\nAccepts plain strings (the common case) or `{ content, metadata }`\nobjects that let providers attach typed metadata (e.g. Anthropic\n`cache_control` for prompt caching) per prompt. At the chat call site\nthe adapter narrows `metadata`'s type via `~types['systemPromptMetadata']`\n— providers that don't declare one default to `never`, which makes the\nfield carry no meaningful value (TypeScript will only accept\n`undefined` there). Provider-foreign metadata that reaches an adapter\nvia JS / `as any` is silently dropped, never written to the wire.\n\n#### See\n\nSystemPrompt\n\n***\n\n### threadId?\n\n```ts\noptional threadId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1232](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1232)\n\nThread ID for AG-UI protocol run correlation.\nWhen provided, this will be used in RunStartedEvent and RunFinishedEvent.\n\n***\n\n### toolExecution?\n\n```ts\noptional toolExecution?: \"parallel\" | \"sequential\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1147](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1147)\n\nHow the server tools of one model turn run. `'parallel'` (the default)\nstarts them together, and `'sequential'` runs them one at a time.\n\n***\n\n### tools?\n\n```ts\noptional tools?: AnyTool[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1121](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1121)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: TextOptions\ntitle: TextOptions\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1114](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1114)\n\nOptions passed into the SDK and further piped to the AI provider.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TProviderOptionsSuperset\n\n`TProviderOptionsSuperset` *extends* `Record`\\<`string`, `any`\\> = `Record`\\<`string`, `any`\\>\n\n### TProviderOptionsForModel\n\n`TProviderOptionsForModel` = `TProviderOptionsSuperset`\n\n### TContext\n\n`TContext` = `unknown`\n\n## Properties\n\n### abortController?\n\n```ts\noptional abortController?: AbortController;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1219](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1219)\n\nAbortController for request cancellation.\n\nAllows you to cancel an in-progress request using an AbortController.\nUseful for implementing timeouts or user-initiated cancellations.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst abortController = new AbortController();\nsetTimeout(() => abortController.abort(), 5000); // Cancel after 5 seconds\nawait chat({ ..., abortController });\n```\n\n#### See\n\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortController\n\n***\n\n### agentLoopStrategy?\n\n```ts\noptional agentLoopStrategy?: AgentLoopStrategy;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1142](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1142)\n\n***\n\n### approvals?\n\n```ts\noptional approvals?: ReadonlyMap<string, boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1277](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1277)\n\nClient approval decisions for this run, keyed by approval id. The engine\npopulates this from approvals carried on the incoming messages. Harness\nadapters consult it to resolve `ask`-policy permission requests (the agent\npauses on a risky action; the client re-runs with a decision recorded\nhere). Undefined for direct adapter usage outside the chat engine.\n\n***\n\n### capabilities?\n\n```ts\noptional capabilities?: CapabilityContext;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1268](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1268)\n\nMiddleware capability context for this run. The engine populates it with\nthe live middleware context so harness adapters that declare\n`requires: [SomeCapability]` can read provided capabilities from inside\n`chatStream` — e.g. `getSandbox(options.capabilities)`. Capabilities are\nprovisioned by middleware `setup` before the adapter runs. Undefined for\ndirect adapter usage outside the chat engine.\n\n***\n\n### context?\n\n```ts\noptional context?: TContext;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1126](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1126)\n\nRuntime context provided by the caller and passed to middleware and\nserver-side tool implementations.\n\n***\n\n### ~~conversationId?~~\n\n```ts\noptional conversationId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1205](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1205)\n\n#### Deprecated\n\nUse `threadId` instead. `conversationId` is the legacy\npre-AG-UI name for the same concept (a stable per-conversation\nidentifier used to correlate client/server devtools events). When\n`conversationId` is omitted, the runtime falls back to `threadId`\nautomatically, so most callers can simply pass `threadId` (or rely\non `chatParamsFromRequest`, which surfaces it on `params`).\n\nWill be removed in a future major release.\n\n***\n\n### lazyToolsConfig?\n\n```ts\noptional lazyToolsConfig?: LazyToolsConfig;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1153](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1153)\n\nOptional configuration for lazy-tool discovery (tools marked `lazy: true`).\nTunes how much of each lazy tool's description appears in the discovery\ncatalog. Optional — defaults to `{ includeDescription: 'none' }`.\n\n***\n\n### logger\n\n```ts\nlogger: InternalLogger;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1226](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1226)\n\nInternal logger threaded from the chat entry point. Adapter implementations\nmust call `logger.request()` before SDK calls, `logger.provider()` for each\nchunk received, and `logger.errors()` in catch blocks.\n\n***\n\n### messages\n\n```ts\nmessages: ModelMessage<\n  | string\n  | ContentPart<unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown>[]\n  | null>[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1120](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1120)\n\n***\n\n### metadata?\n\n```ts\noptional metadata?: Record<string, any>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1164](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1164)\n\nObservability metadata attached to this call. Surfaced to middleware,\ndevtools, and the event client; values may be arbitrarily structured\n(objects, arrays). Adapters never forward this field onto the provider\nwire request.\n\nTo send provider-side request metadata, use the provider's\n`modelOptions` field instead, where the provider supports one (e.g.\nOpenAI's and OpenRouter's `metadata` are both Record<string, string>).\n\n***\n\n### model\n\n```ts\nmodel: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1119](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1119)\n\n***\n\n### modelOptions?\n\n```ts\noptional modelOptions?: TProviderOptionsForModel;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1165](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1165)\n\n***\n\n### outputSchema?\n\n```ts\noptional outputSchema?: SchemaInput;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1194](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1194)\n\nSchema for structured output.\n\n**Two distinct use sites:**\n\n1. **User-facing (activity layer):** accepts any\n   [SchemaInput](../type-aliases/SchemaInput.md) — Zod, ArkType, Valibot, or a raw JSON Schema.\n   The activity layer converts to JSON Schema before handing off.\n\n2. **Adapter-facing (`chatStream` call):** the engine populates this with\n   a pre-converted JSON Schema **only** when the adapter declared\n   `supportsCombinedToolsAndSchema(modelOptions) === true`. The adapter\n   should then wire the schema into the upstream request (e.g.\n   `response_format: { type: 'json_schema', ... }`, `text.format`,\n   `output_format`, `--json-schema`) alongside any `tools`.\n\n   How the engine then takes the object depends on\n   `combinedStructuredOutputSource()`:\n   - `'text'` (default): the final-turn assistant text is the JSON.\n   - `'event'`: the adapter emits `structured-output.complete` during\n     `chatStream`. Accumulated prose is not parsed.\n\n   Adapters that did NOT declare the capability never see this field\n   populated — the engine instead invokes `structuredOutput` /\n   `structuredOutputStream` after the agent loop.\n\n***\n\n### parentRunId?\n\n```ts\noptional parentRunId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1243](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1243)\n\nParent run ID for AG-UI protocol nested run correlation.\nSurfaced for observability/middleware; not consumed by the LLM call.\n\n***\n\n### request?\n\n```ts\noptional request?: Request | RequestInit;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1166](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1166)\n\n***\n\n### resume?\n\n```ts\noptional resume?: RunAgentResumeItem[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1258](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1258)\n\nAG-UI interrupt resume responses supplied by the client on a follow-up run.\nA first-party generic item carries the original request in `metadata`.\n\n***\n\n### runId?\n\n```ts\noptional runId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1238](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1238)\n\nRun ID for AG-UI protocol run correlation.\nWhen provided, this will be used in RunStartedEvent and RunFinishedEvent.\nIf not provided, a unique ID will be generated.\n\n***\n\n### state?\n\n```ts\noptional state?: unknown;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1252](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1252)\n\nApplication state mirrored in a STATE_SNAPSHOT before an interrupt terminal.\n\n***\n\n### subagentRunId?\n\n```ts\noptional subagentRunId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1249](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1249)\n\nAG-UI subagent run id when this chat runs as a child of another run.\nA child `chat()` passes `ctx.subagentRunId`. Middleware reads it as\n`ctx.subagentRunId`. Absent on a top-level run.\n\n***\n\n### systemPrompts?\n\n```ts\noptional systemPrompts?: SystemPrompt[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1141](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1141)\n\nSystem prompts to include with the request.\n\nAccepts plain strings (the common case) or `{ content, metadata }`\nobjects that let providers attach typed metadata (e.g. Anthropic\n`cache_control` for prompt caching) per prompt. At the chat call site\nthe adapter narrows `metadata`'s type via `~types['systemPromptMetadata']`\n— providers that don't declare one default to `never`, which makes the\nfield carry no meaningful value (TypeScript will only accept\n`undefined` there). Provider-foreign metadata that reaches an adapter\nvia JS / `as any` is silently dropped, never written to the wire.\n\n#### See\n\nSystemPrompt\n\n***\n\n### threadId?\n\n```ts\noptional threadId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1232](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1232)\n\nThread ID for AG-UI protocol run correlation.\nWhen provided, this will be used in RunStartedEvent and RunFinishedEvent.\n\n***\n\n### toolExecution?\n\n```ts\noptional toolExecution?: \"parallel\" | \"sequential\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1147](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1147)\n\nHow the server tools of one model turn run. `'parallel'` (the default)\nstarts them together, and `'sequential'` runs them one at a time.\n\n***\n\n### tools?\n\n```ts\noptional tools?: AnyTool[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1121](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1121)\n"}
